      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fawnskin%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1924, composer Fannie Charles Dillon founded Woodland Theater in Fawnskin, serving as its general manager until 1929.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fawnskin%2C_California",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fawnskin was once a thriving artists’ colony that drew composers, musicians, and actors from Los Angeles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fawnskin%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s historic Old Miller School House Park is one of three community parks that preserve the area’s heritage.",
